invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_vector.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: the last group multiplies both lanes by r^4 and r^2, as every
  group before it does, so the odd blocks of the last group, and every
  odd block before them, are owed one power of r more than they get. The
  tag is wrong for every update the path takes. CBMC cannot read an
  intrinsic, so no proof covers this file, and bin/poly1305_equiv_test
  holds its accumulator to poly1305.c's after every update.

--- old
    multiplier_set(&of_r.first, of_r.r4, of_r.r3);
    multiplier_set(&of_r.second, of_r.r2, p->r);
--- new
    multiplier_set(&of_r.first, of_r.r4, of_r.r4);
    multiplier_set(&of_r.second, of_r.r2, of_r.r2);
